  "name": "rust-docs-mcp",
  "description": "A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server providing comprehensive, offline-capable access to Rust crate documentation, source code analysis, and dependency graphs. It leverages rustdoc JSON generation and the Tantivy search engine to enable high-fidelity programmatic exploration of crate internals, including module hierarchies and type relationships. The system facilitates deep understanding for AI agents through optimized local caching and indexing of crates sourced from crates.io, GitHub, or local directories.",
